Laundry Service Responsive Website

Project Overview

This project is a responsive **Laundry Service Website** created using **HTML and CSS**. The webpage provides a simple and attractive interface for a laundry service where users can view services, learn about the company, and book a service.

The website is designed to work on different screen sizes such as desktop, tablet, and mobile devices.

Technologies Used

* HTML5
* CSS3
* CSS Media Queries
* Responsive Web Design

Features

* Responsive navigation bar
* Website logo
* Home, Services, About Us, and Contact Us links
* Username button
* Attractive hero section
* Laundry service heading and description
* "Book a service today!" button
* Laundry-related image
* Mobile responsive layout
* Flexible design using CSS

Project Structure

```text
Laundry-Service/
│
├── index.html
├── Style1.css
├── image.png
└── README.md
```

Main Files

index.html

Contains the complete structure of the webpage, including:

* Header
* Navigation bar
* Hero section
* Text content
* Image
* Booking button

Style1.css

Contains the styling and responsive design of the webpage, including:

* Layout
* Colors
* Fonts
* Spacing
* Buttons
* Image positioning
* Mobile media queries

image.png

This is the laundry-related image displayed in the hero section.

Responsive Design

The website uses a CSS media query for smaller screens:

```css
@media (max-width: 770px)
```

This adjusts the navigation, text size, image size, and button layout for mobile and tablet devices.

How to Run

1. Download or clone the project.
2. Keep `index.html`, `Style1.css`, and `image.png` in the same folder.
3. Open the folder in VS Code.
4. Open `index.html` using a browser or VS Code Live Server.
5. The website will be displayed in the browser.

Purpose

The main purpose of this project is to demonstrate the implementation of a modern and responsive webpage using HTML and CSS. It also demonstrates how media queries can be used to make a website adaptable to different screen sizes.

